            "Skill has grown steadily, by about a day per decade: a 5-day forecast today is about as accurate as a 3-day forecast was 20 years ago. Hurricane track forecasts have improved by two thirds since 1990. A new revolution started in 2023, when machine-learning models trained on decades of reanalysis (GraphCast, Pangu-Weather and others, and the ECMWF's AIFS) began to match or beat the physics-based models on many scores, and run in under a minute on a single processor.",
